        <section id="faqs" class="py-3">
            <h2 class="pipe">Frequently Asked Questions About Services in Harvard, MA</h2>
            
            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How does S. Phaneuf & Associates handle steep slope driveway paving in Harvard, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates grades the driveway subgrade to establish controlled slope angles, installs heavy geotextile stabilization fabric, and compacts an 8-inch crushed stone base. Crews apply a two-course asphalt paving structure consisting of a dense binder layer and a high-traction top course. Extruded asphalt Cape Cod berms or concrete swales are installed along the slope perimeter to capture and divert heavy rainwater runoff, protecting the driveway edge from erosion.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: What types of stone masonry are best suited for Harvard, MA residential properties?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates recommends natural New England fieldstone, thermal bluestone, or granite veneers for outdoor living spaces in Harvard. Natural stone possesses superior density and low absorption rates, making natural stone highly resistant to spalling and cracking caused by winter freeze-thaw cycles. Masons lay stone over deep, gravel-drained concrete footings to ensure structural permanence in Worcester County soils.</p>
